start.README.md:
# transit

The database is SQLite; every function takes an open `sqlite3.Connection` that the caller owns.

## `store.unknown_stop_codes(conn, codes)`

Which of the requested codes are not in the table.

`codes` is a list of strings. Returns those that do not occur in the `stop_name` column of `stops`, in the order given (repeats stay).

The tables hold tens of thousands of rows in production and the database is reached over a slow network
filesystem, so the number of statements (and commits) a call issues matters more than anything else.

```sql
CREATE TABLE routes (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE stops (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, route_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES routes(id), stop_name TEXT NOT NULL, planned INTEGER NOT NULL);
CREATE INDEX idx_stops_route_id ON stops(route_id);
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_stops_code ON stops(stop_name);
```

